    "canonical_ref": "GregNyss.Let.7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If they who run to conjurers or diviners, do it through unbelief, they shall be treated as they who wilfully lapse, but if through want of sense, and through a vain hope of being relieved under their necessities, they shall be treated as those who lapse through the violence of torment.",
